WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Read this French sentence:
«Je crains qu'il ne soit

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.580
trop tard.» It starts with a fear.

3
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.240
But is the speaker afraid it's too late?

4
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.510
Or afraid it's not too late?

5
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.520
Those are opposite fears.

6
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.560
And English 'hardly'.

7
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.750
How would you even squeeze
that into a French sentence?

8
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.660
Two letters, N, E, normally help
turn a French sentence negative.

9
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.870
So when do they mean nothing at all,

10
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.080
and how do you say 'hardly'?

11
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.030
In this mission, you'll
hold sentences up to a meter

12
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.460
to test whether they're really negative.

13
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.360
Then you'll drag «jamais»,
«personne» and «rien» into place

14
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.160
in the negative builder.

15
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.210
Your mission: catch the
negative that isn't one,

16
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.200
and find the French for 'hardly'.
